<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tē^trarches</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράρχης,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a ruler who
				governed the fourth part of a country</i>, <i>a
				tetrarch;</i> in gen., <i>the title of a petty
				prince</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 2, 9, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Phil. 11</span></i>, 
			 12, 31; <i><span class="en">id. Balb. 5, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Mil. 28,
				76</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Deiot. 9, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 3,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 20, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
			51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 15, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				3, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 7, 227</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 5, 7</span></i>.—Also
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tē^trar-cha</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Matt. 14, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Luc. 3, 19</span></i>.</div>
